<div class="rev3"><div class="ct">★ AND A LOSING RIDER IS STRUCTURALLY SILENT — that is the real defect</div><p>The reason this ran for six hours is that nothing was shouting. The rider pages on peak give-back and on stalls; below its arm threshold there is no stop, no trail and no alert, so a position that is simply losing produces no output at all. Both of the tools you would naturally check print &ldquo;flat, $0&rdquo; while it happens, because the trade has not CLOSED yet and they count closed rows.</p><p><strong>The rehabilitation of the rider is not an entry change and it is not a threshold change. It is a stop.</strong> A 1.5&times;ATR protective stop on the rider's own book, sized off its entry ATR, is the single highest-value change on this week's card and the table above prices it at about $1,000 on one day.</p></div>

