<h2><span class="n">P1.6</span> THE DAY RIDER &mdash; the week of 17&ndash;21 August 2026</h2>

<p class="lead">Gaz, the two books swapped places. Last week the rider made <strong>+$1,617.50 on five
trades</strong> while the tournament lost $325.00; this week the tournament is a rounding error at
<strong>&minus;$4.50 on 36 lots</strong> and <strong>the rider is the loss</strong>. It closed seven legs
for <strong>&minus;$169.50</strong> in the strategy book, <strong>&minus;$251.00</strong> in cash.</p>

<p class="lead">But that headline hides the thing worth knowing. Split the book by <em>who pressed the
button</em> and it separates cleanly: the <strong>automatic rider went 3&ndash;1 for &minus;$100.50</strong>
across four sessions, and <strong>every other dollar of damage came from a hand</strong> &mdash; two manual
entries on Friday, one killed by a bug sixty seconds after it was placed, the other
<strong>still open right now</strong> because the IB gateway wedged at 19:58Z and the 20:40 hard flat
never ran.</p>

<div class="callout"><div class="ct">THE ONE-PARAGRAPH VERSION</div>
<p><strong>Realised &minus;$169.50 (strategy) / &minus;$251.00 (cash), plus a 4-lot long marked
&minus;$973.00 that is UNRESOLVED as I write.</strong>
<strong>ENTRIES:</strong> all four automatic confirmations landed inside the validated 13:38&ndash;14:09
window; the two entries outside it were both manual and both are under water.
<strong>THRESHOLDS:</strong> nothing to change. The margins ran +0.006 to +0.490 over the ER floor, and
I probed the floors directly &mdash; raising ER to 0.20 <em>and</em> RT to 0.55 removes <strong>zero</strong>
fires this week, it only makes them <strong>later and worse</strong>, by &minus;$116 and &minus;$156 on the
two it touches.
<strong>EXITS:</strong> the operator's claims took <strong>91.0% and 89.3%</strong> of everything available on
the two winners he claimed and beat the machine trail by <strong>+$180.29</strong>; the one mechanical TRAIL
took <strong>36.7%</strong>; on the losing day the claims cost <strong>&minus;$120.50</strong> against just
letting the clock do it.
<strong>THE WEAK DAY IS THURSDAY 08-20 and it is a FAULT, not a drought</strong> &mdash; the tape offered
<strong>$1,158</strong> on the short side and the rider bought the high of the day
<strong>37 seconds after it printed</strong>.</p></div>

