<p class="ln">The loose trigger is negative in and out of sample, which is clean. The derived
trigger is the interesting one: &minus;$147.00 in-sample and
<strong>$655.00 out-of-sample on 79 fires over
226 sessions</strong>. An arm that does better out of sample than in is
usually a good sign.</p>

<div class="rev3"><div class="ct">★ BUT THE DIRECTIONAL CONTROL KILLS IT, AND IT HAS TO BE SAID ON THE SAME PAGE</div><p>The same out-of-sample window carries a plain directional control: hold gold LONG every session and you lose <strong>&minus;$21,738.00</strong>; hold it SHORT every session and you make <strong>$20,382.00</strong>, over 226 sessions.</p><p>The gold rider's out-of-sample $655.00 is a rounding error against a $20,382 short drift sitting underneath it. Any gold arm that is even slightly short-biased will look profitable on this window without carrying one gram of edge. <strong>Every gold result in this report needs its long/short mix reported next to it, and none of them currently do.</strong> That is a method fix, it is on the BUILD card, and until it lands no gold arm should be promoted to anything.</p></div>

