<p class="ln">The open rider, replayed across 229 sessions at two lots, loses
$20,739.00. Split it by the window lead and the &ldquo;inside&rdquo; population
makes $825.00 on 60 sessions while &ldquo;outside&rdquo; loses
$21,564.00 on 165. That looks like the window is the whole story
until the strip-best-3 column: the inside population goes to &minus;$7,745.00.
<strong>Three sessions are the entire lead.</strong> REFUTED as a session filter on this evidence.</p>

<p class="ln">The stay-out meter's direction call, on the same population: when its two reads
agree it is right 51.7% of the time over 178 sessions, which is a
coin. Split by call, its UP calls hit 56.7% and its DOWN calls
45.7% &mdash; and that gap is the same short drift the gold control just
exposed, not skill. The 51 mixed-signal sessions average
&minus;$20.79. The corrected series (231 sessions) says the same thing to within a
point. <strong>The meter is a stay-out instrument and it should not be read as a direction
instrument</strong>, which is exactly what it says on its own label and exactly what keeps getting
forgotten.</p>

