<section id="sec8"><h2><span class="n">M3</span> The greenfield lab &mdash; we can see the runs coming, we still cannot tell which way they go</h2>

<p class="lead">Movement&nbsp;1 froze the tape: <strong>70 big runs on MNQ this week, 65 of them sat out, carrying $9,986 of one-lot hindsight ceiling</strong>. This movement ignores every gate we own and asks whether a brand-new entry could have taken any of it. The answer this week is a <strong>NULL on MNQ and one thin survivor on gold</strong> &mdash; but it is a null with three hard numbers behind it, and they say something different from "nothing works". <strong>First: the money is real and the exit is not the problem.</strong> Board all 65 sat-out runs at their own start, in the right direction, with a purely mechanical 3&times;ATR stop and 6&times;ATR target, and it banks <strong>+$4,009 over 45 trades at +$89.09 each, 84.4% wins &mdash; 40.1% of the entire ceiling, converted by the exit alone</strong>. <strong>Second: we can board them.</strong> A dumb causal detector &mdash; "the last ten minutes covered two ATRs one way" &mdash; boards <strong>50 of the 65 in the right direction, a median six minutes in, with a median 42 points still on the table</strong>. <strong>Third, and this is the whole problem: the same detector fires 155 times in the same five days, and only 50 of those fires are runs.</strong> The 50 that are runs made +$483. The other 105 lost &minus;$1,651. <strong>Detection is solved. Selection is not.</strong> And the size threshold the mandate asked us to find is real, sharp and sits at <strong>120 points</strong> &mdash; below it, boarding a run loses money at every band; at and above it, boarding pays <strong>+$69.38 a trade over 51 trades and survives strip-3, strip-5, leave-one-day-out and long/short symmetry</strong>. It is a hindsight band, and closing that gap is next week's entire job.</p>

<div class="callout"><div class="ct">LEAD WITH WHAT SURVIVED</div>
<p>Five things walked out of this movement alive. Everything else is in the graves table, by name, with the test that killed it.</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>★ THE SIZE THRESHOLD IS 120 POINTS, and it is the deliverable the mandate asked for.</strong> Rebuilding the census picker over the whole lake gives <strong>686 runs on 33 trading days</strong> &mdash; real n, not fifteen. Board each one at its own first fire and the answer is not gradual, it is a step: <strong>55&ndash;70pt loses $12.10 a trade, 70&ndash;90pt loses $6.35, 90&ndash;120pt loses $9.48 &mdash; and then 120&ndash;160pt makes +$54.04 and 160pt+ makes +$86.64.</strong> Pooled at 120pt+: <strong>n=51, +$3,538, +$69.38 a trade, 52.9% wins</strong>, strip-3 still +$1,940, strip-5 still +$1,051, worst leave-one-day-out +$2,357, and both sides pay (long +$74.82, short +$64.91). That is the most robust thing this movement has produced in three Fridays.</li>
<li><strong>The exit is exonerated.</strong> The desk keeps re-litigating exits. On this population the exit does 40.1% of the ceiling on its own. Whatever is wrong, it is not the stop and it is not the target.</li>
<li><strong>★ The one stone last Friday named for "next week" &mdash; the large-lot / small-lot aggressor split &mdash; is TURNED, and it is not empty.</strong> It is a null on direction like everything else (large-lot flow agrees with the next 15 minutes <strong>48.71%</strong> of the time on unselected big moves, against price's 48.66% and L2's 49.44%) &mdash; but <strong>SMALL</strong>-lot flow is inversely informative and it strengthens monotonically with size: <strong>49.56% on all minutes &rarr; 48.50% at 30pt &rarr; 46.57% at 55pt &rarr; 44.31% at 90pt &rarr; 42.95% at 120pt</strong>. Fading the retail tape reads 57.05% on the biggest moves. And <strong>|large-lot flow| detects size better than anything VACUUM found: AUC 0.721 (p&lt;0.0001) on the 120pt+ band</strong>, against volume-z's 0.690. Both findings are real. Neither trades &mdash; see the graves.</li>
<li><strong>One gold cell survived its forward test.</strong> Last week's <code>mgc_hole_break_fade</code> double-hole refinement made <strong>+$159 over 27 trades (+$5.88 each) on the five days it had never seen</strong>, green on 3 of 5. Everything else in gold died, including its own simpler primary arm. It stays SHADOW on thin n.</li>
<li><strong>Every candidate that survived last Friday on MNQ is now dead, and they were killed by the same test.</strong> BREAKFLOW, the pooled rider mechanism and VAC-ABS all went forward onto 08-17&ndash;08-21 and all three lost. That is not three coincidences; it is the selection problem showing up on schedule.</li>
