<h3>1. The oracle &mdash; the money is real, and the exit is not what is broken</h3>

<p>Before inventing anything, the cheapest possible question: <em>if we knew everything, what would the exit hand back?</em> So I took each of the 65 sat-out runs, entered at its own start minute in its own direction, and let the desk's most ordinary wide exit run &mdash; stop 3&times;ATR, target 6&times;ATR, two-hour cap, one position at a time, full costs. No filter, no cleverness, no hindsight in the exit at all. Just: <em>could a mechanical exit convert a hindsight ceiling into money?</em></p>

