<p><strong>Chop-lab verdict: DO NOT BUILD A CHOP-TURN SCALPER.</strong> Not because chop is untradeable in principle, but because the specific thing that would have to be true &mdash; that the resting book separates a turn from a break at a range extreme &mdash; is measurably false at two fidelities across 8,386 model-free races, and because the desk is not losing money in the chop anyway. <strong>The real lead is a bench, not a gate, and it is worth roughly $5,400 gross over eighteen days.</strong> The single most valuable backtest anyone could run off this lab is the counterfactual: what would benching those blocks have cost in winners forgone?</p>

